A162 — how swift-format is obtained, and what the gates actually need
Host: 27.0 / arm64

--- The hole, demonstrated: every tool but swift-format on PATH ---
$ env PATH=<tmp with swift, swiftlint, xcrun, jq, node> bash tools/audit-checks.sh
missing required tool: swift-format (see AUDIT/environment.md)
exit=2

$ env PATH=<same> xcrun --find swift-format
/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Toolchains/XcodeDefault.xctoolchain/usr/bin/swift-format
exit=0

A reader who believed the old record — "swift-format comes from Xcode 27 (xcrun swift-format); it is not
installed from brew for this audit" — would have Xcode's, believe the environment was complete, and get
exit 2 with `missing required tool: swift-format` from the gate.

--- What is actually installed and what the gates run ---
  command -v swift-format : /opt/homebrew/bin/swift-format
  resolves to             : ../Cellar/swift-format/603.0.0/bin/swift-format
  swift-format --version  : 603.0.0 (the one on PATH, so the one both gates run)
  xcrun swift-format -v   : main
  xcrun --find swift-format: /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Toolchains/XcodeDefault.xctoolchain/usr/bin/swift-format
  brew list --versions    : swift-format 603.0.0

--- Both builds, on the same tree, today ---
  brew 603.0.0 : 739 diagnostics
  xcrun main   : 739 diagnostics

--- What the gates require ---
  tools/audit-checks.sh:42  the required-tool loop: for tool in swift swiftlint swift-format xcrun jq node
  tools/audit-checks.sh:43  command -v "\$tool"
  AUDIT/phase-e.sh:332  if command -v swift-format

